<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's AAPT says equity raising is an option.</title>
<headline>Australia's AAPT says equity raising is an option.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>AAPT Telecommunications Pty Ltd said on Monday that an equity raising was one of several options the telecommunications group was looking at to fund its planned rollout of infrastructure projects.</p>
<p>&quot;That (equity raising) is one of the options we are looking at, along with some strategic partnering and some other options,&quot; AAPT chief executive officer Larry Williams told Reuters after a news conference.</p>
<p>Williams said any new funding would be used to finance the expansion of its infrastructure in order to offer new services under a newly deregulated Australian telecommunications market.</p>
</text>
